        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a5a14fe4-45f5-5f0f-954a-105d94e0cab4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akshay Kumar, Nagarjuna, Pooja Bhatt, Sonali Bendre, Anu Malik, Aadesh Shrivastava\n- Films: Angaaray, Kash Aap Hamare Hote, Lahu Ke Do Rang, Insaaf, Daava, Tarazu, Barood, Zulmi\n- Topics: film music, box office performance, death\n\nFacts:\n- The 1998 film Angaaray stars Akshay Kumar, Nagarjuna, Pooja Bhatt, and Sonali Bendre in lead roles.\n- The music for Angaaray was composed by Anu Malik and Aadesh Shrivastava.\n- In the 1990s, Akshay Kumar's releases Lahu Ke Do Rang, Insaaf, Daava, Tarazu, Angaaray, Barood, and Zulmi performed poorly at the box office, causing a setback in his film career.\n- Aadesh Shrivastava composed the original music for Kash Aap Hamare Hote.\n- A day after turning 51, Aadesh Shrivastava died of cancer at Kokilaben Hospital.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6e21fb84-89a1-5d3e-86c0-0df5baba2a27",
        "text": "Page: Angaaray (1998 film). Sentence: It stars Akshay Kumar, Nagarjuna, Pooja Bhatt, Sonali Bendre in lead roles and music is composed by Anu Malik & Aadesh Shrivastava.\nPage: Aadesh Shrivastava. Sentence: Just a day after he turned 51, he died of cancer in Kokilaben Hospital.\nPage: Akshay Kumar filmography. Sentence: However, several other of his releases in the 1990s, including \"Lahu Ke Do Rang\", \"Insaaf\", \"Daava\", \"Tarazu\", \"Angaaray\", \"Barood\" and \"Zulmi\" performed poorly at the box office leading to a setback in his film career.\nPage: Kash Aap Hamare Hote. Sentence: The original music is by Aadesh Shrivastava.",
